# The build context of crates/apassy-relay/Dockerfile is the repository root. Only the
# files that `cargo build -p apassy-relay` reads go in: the workspace manifests and
# lock, the Cargo settings, the core crate (its sources, rule packs, sandbox profiles,
# and the test and example targets that its manifest names), the iOS core member, the
# app member (Cargo loads every workspace member, even for `-p apassy-relay`), and
# this crate. rust-toolchain.toml stays out: the image already has Rust 1.97.0.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.cargo/config.toml
!src/
!packs/
!sandbox/
!tests/
!examples/
!benches/
!ios/ApassyCore/Cargo.toml
!ios/ApassyCore/src/
!crates/apassy-app/Cargo.toml
!crates/apassy-app/src/
!crates/apassy-app/tests/
!crates/apassy-relay/Cargo.toml
!crates/apassy-relay/src/
!crates/apassy-relay/vendor/
!crates/apassy-relay/examples/
!crates/apassy-relay/tests/
